    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on exploiting high-ceiling matchups against weak arms, led by **Josh Naylor** (78.46) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21). Both benefit immensely from a favorable encounter with Paez, whose 9.12 xERA creates a target-rich environment for our corner infielders. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) also registers as a must-start; his high-efficiency score is driven by a massive 14% park factor boost and a plus-matchup against Bradish. While **Corbin Carroll** (52.77) and **Gabriel Moreno** (44.52) face a stiffer test against Luzardo, their role in the heart of the order and our organizational mandate to chase speed keeps **Corbin Carroll** in the lineup despite the SP's stingy nature.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Isaac Paredes** (55.38), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Jose Caballero**. While **Isaac Paredes** posted a stronger individual profile, **Jose Caballero** remains vital to our strategy in the scarcest category\u2014stolen bases\u2014and his potential for late-game disruptive speed outweighs the marginal gap in pure projection. Elsewhere, **Seiya Suzuki** (64.83) and **Griffin Conine** (61.48) represent solid mid-tier plays, with **Griffin Conine** benefiting from favorable winds and a vulnerable arm in Dobnak. We are monitoring **Gabriel Moreno** and **Jose Caballero** closely, as both carry \"Lineup Pending\" tags; should they drop lower in the order than assumed, we will re-evaluate our utility depth, though the current floor for **Edwin Arroyo** (51.85) remains safe enough to avoid dropping below our 40-point threshold.",
